cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this result, please cite the tagged release.
title: "Three disjoint doublings for two theta prime races"
abstract: "Three common starting heights, including one prescribed integer, reproduce four level and move targets on the 547/727 and 571/599 prime races. Their doublings are disjoint and each weight exceeds 1/400. Direct prime-ideal calculations prove the finite theorem. A local inverse has exact generic degree four. The late recurrence uses the critical-line result for the sixteen primitive odd Dirichlet factors."
